cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this platform, please cite it as below and cite the underlying tools."
title: "Two Therapeutic Strategies to Target KRAS Mutants: an open, end-to-end computational platform for small-molecule screening and ADAR RNA editing in pancreatic cancer"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nguyen
    given-names: Truong
    affiliation: "CUNY School of Medicine"
repository-code: "https://github.com/truong128/two-strategies-to-target-kras-mutants"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - KRAS mutants
  - pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma
  - ultra-large virtual screening
  - machine learning
  - ADAR
  - RNA editing
  - Nextflow
abstract: >-
  Reproducible computational workflows against KRAS mutants: ML-guided docking of a 13.6 billion molecule
  library with resistance-aware ensemble docking, Boltz-2, molecular dynamics, MM/GBSA and retrosynthesis;
  ADAR-recruiting guide RNA design with off-target and structure stages; and peptide binder design for 18
  KRAS alleles (mutants). Code and protocols only; no data or results are distributed.
